Think about the following task. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {0, 1, 4, 1, -3};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > 0) acc++;
return acc;

Take a moment to solve this. What does this string routine return?
String s = "ybycd";
StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) out.append(s.charAt(i));
return out.toString();

Work through the problem below. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {1, 5, 8, 12, 14, 18};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 6) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 6) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Given the details below, respond. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(15);
Node b = new Node(35);
Node c = new Node(30);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Examine the case described here. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {6, 11, 16, 21, 26, 27, 32, 34, 35, 38, 43};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 16) return mid; if (a[mid] < 16) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return -1;

